      "writtenOn": "2024-07-31T21:18:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should be fine, it makes the assumption that a module will be built on a given thread and not multiple threads, but i think that\u0027s fine. As long as the number goes up it doesn\u0027t matter.",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7576a67f_480df16e",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/instruction.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T16:52:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is safe in the presence of multi-threading, as the race between two different threads compiling two different modules will break the guarantee that this counter is monotonically increasing.\n\nYou /could/ make it thread local if we think we can guarantee that a module will only ever be handled by a single thread, but I\u0027m not sure we can guarantee that.\n\nI think it would be safer to put the counter on the module, and have all instruction creation go via a helper function on the module, which passes the ID to the constructor.",
      "parentUuid": "b8cfc3ac_1ff60b99",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99037c4c_729dcfdc",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/instruction.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003216
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T16:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t matter if you compile two modules on two threads and the IDs conflict, you\u0027d never combine them. I don\u0027t see a world where we build half a module on one thread and half on another and somehow combine them. Maybe if you compiled the module on one thread, ran some transforms there, passed to a second thread and ran another bunch of transforms on it? But even that seems unlikely?\n\nEven in the module it isn\u0027t safe to build the module on two threads as it won\u0027t be locked. It would allow passing to another thread to run some transforms if we want.",
      "parentUuid": "7576a67f_480df16e",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59315565_2371dec4",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/instruction.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T17:30:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could also make the static var a `std::atomic\u003cuint32_t\u003e` here, and you\u0027d get the guaranteed monotonically increasing value.",
      "parentUuid": "99037c4c_729dcfdc",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "915ad6e3_3441b277",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/instruction.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T17:33:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, `std::atomic` would be the way to avoid multiple threads breaking the guarantee that a single module needs, but that has some performance impact.\n\nDan: The issue isn\u0027t that IDs conflict between two modules on two threads, it\u0027s that having two threads concurrently incrementing the same counter (non-atomically) will lead to the IDs not being monotonically increasing within a single module.\n\nI can also imagine a world where we convert from AST-\u003eIR on one thread (shader module creation), and then do backend codegen on a different thread (pipeline creation). I don\u0027t know whether these two operations are already running on different threads in Dawn or not.",
      "parentUuid": "59315565_2371dec4",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43ea5fe7_4a21d127",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/core/ir/instruction.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003216
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T17:36:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Monotonic doesn\u0027t matter, as long as they are increasing. We don\u0027t care if a module is {1,2,3} or {1,6,10} as long as they go up.\n\nDawn is currently single threaded, thought they are talking about multi-threading. I\u0027m not sure if that would mean createShaderModule vs createPipeline happening on different threads or not thought.",
      "parentUuid": "915ad6e3_3441b277",
      "revId": "318539882c43172a83dac6ef0e1ad30d6fe1666e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
